{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "A>=B test corpus of polynomial inequalities. Each entry is tagged by category and by the status v1 of the prover is expected to return. Entries with an 'sos' field carry an exact sum-of-squares certificate over Q and are machine-verified by corpus/verify.py against the trusted checker; if a certificate verifies, the stated inequality is proven true for all real values.",
  "categories": {
    "in_scope_sos": "Holds for all real values and is provable by a sum-of-squares certificate over Q. The target for the v1 prover. Should return PROVED once the prover exists; carries an exact 'sos' certificate today.",
    "out_of_scope_v1": "A true inequality that needs side constraints (positivity, abc=1, a+b+c=k, triangle sides, ...) and so is NOT nonnegative for all reals. Out of scope for the v1 SOS-over-R engine; v1 should return NO_CERT_FOUND, never PROVED.",
    "not_sos": "Nonnegative for all reals but NOT a sum of squares (Motzkin / Choi-Lam family). A soundness test: the SOS engine must return NO_CERT_FOUND, never PROVED.",
    "false": "A deliberately false inequality. Soundness test: the prover must never return PROVED."
  },
  "expected_values": ["PROVED", "NO_CERT_FOUND"],
  "sources": [
    "Evan Chen, 'A Brief Introduction to Olympiad Inequalities' (web.evanchen.cc/handouts/Ineq/en.pdf)",
    "Evan Chen, 'Supersums of Square-Weights (SOS)' (web.evanchen.cc/handouts/SOS-Dumbass/SOS-Dumbass.pdf)",
    "R. B. Manfrino, J. A. G. Ortega, R. V. Delgado, 'Inequalities: A Mathematical Olympiad Approach' (Birkhauser, 2009)",
    "Art of Problem Solving (artofproblemsolving.com) community and olympiad archives",
    "Classical results: AM-GM, Cauchy-Schwarz / Lagrange identity, Schur, QM-AM (variance)"
  ],
